  "question": {
    "text": "If the number of solutions of the equation <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo></math> where <math><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></math> is <math><mi>k</mi></math>, then <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2.4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo></math> where <math><mi>h</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo></math> where <math><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />Then,&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />When <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then there are <math><mn>8</mn></math> ways.<br />When <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then there are <math><mn>6</mn></math> ways.<br />When <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then there are <math><mn>5</mn></math> ways.<br />When <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then there are <math><mn>3</mn></math> ways.<br />When <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then there are <math><mn>2</mn></math> ways.<br />When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> not possible.<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Total number of ways <math><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math>"
  }
